From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 03:42:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ac: GetConnectingLocation (0x0014), value from a hidden
 setting

Animal Crossing: New Leaf calls ac:u 0x0014 (GetConnectingLocation,
undocumented) at the post office right after connecting, then reads the
current access point, to decide whether a Nintendo Zone gift can be
handed out ("It seems the present isn't being delivered with the access
point you're connected to right now."). The command wasn't in the
handler table, so the generic fallback replied and the game read leftover
request data (0x0C, the ProcessID placeholder) as the answer.

It now replies with a result and a u32. The meaning of the values is
unknown, so the value comes from a hidden setting,
[WebService] ac_connecting_location (default 0), which can be changed in
the config file to find the value that means "Nintendo Zone". Every call
is logged at Info level. Registered on ac:u and ac:i.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FYz3krf43qKGY6aS2Z5snz
